   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 1.3. Increased institutional capacity of labour administrations</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">In 2021, the Ministry of Labour and Social Affairs completed a mapping of the labour inspection procedural workflow of the five regional Bureaus of Labour and Social Affairs (BOLSAs) and the Ministry itself. Based on the mapping, the inspectorates in the ministry and five Bureaus have defined new standardised labour inspection procedures and are implementing them throughout the five Bureaus and the Ministry. There is a new defined procedure to initiate court proceedings with templates that is being implemented by the Ministry and Bureaus. Through the ONEILO Advancing Decent Work Programme, support is provided to the Ministry of Labour and Social Affairs (MOLSA) on three complementary interventions to strengthen the labour inspection system in Ethiopia. 
The programme is working with MOLSA and Regional BOLSAs to develop a labour inspection information and a knowledge management system. The system will make the enforcement efficient, effective and transparent as it ease internal and external reporting, standardize the collection and analysis of statistics, and facilitate evidence-based planning and identification of priority compliance issues and targets.
Before developing the system, mapping and standardizing the labour inspection workflow is essential.
Hence, the programme in collaboration with HQ LABADMIN-OSH facilitated the mapping of the labour inspection workflow of the ministry and five bureaus; provided technical support to identify gaps in the procedure and to design new procedure; and delivered technical support to standardise the procedure. The programme organized a validation workshop for labour inspectorates from the Ministry and Bureaus to validate the procedure and train labour inspectors on the standardized labour inspection procedure.</narrative>
   </description>
